Here is the hard truth about why a screenshot cannot save you if you handle the trade incorrectly, and how the platform actually handles disputes:
## 1. The Platform Does Not Insure Your Trades
Crypto exchanges like Binance, NoOnes, or Bybit are only middlemen (escrow providers). They do not hold pools of cash to compensate traders who fall victim to mobile money reversals. Once customer support closes an appeal and releases the crypto from escrow to the buyer's wallet, that crypto is on the blockchain and gone forever. The platform cannot pull it back. [2] 
## 2. A Screenshot is Not Definitive Proof to a Crypto Platform
If a buyer initiates an MTN MoMo self-reversal (*126# -> Option 7 -> Option 5) after you have already released the crypto, opening a late dispute with just a screenshot of your previous balance will not automatically get you a refund. [3] 

* 
* Screenshots are easily faked: Scammers use spoofing apps to generate fake transaction receipts and fake balance screens.
* The Platform needs a Statement: To prove a reversal actually happened after a trade was completed, the platform's support team will reject screenshots. They will demand a PDF copy of your official MTN MoMo transaction statement or a video recording of you logging into your live MTN MoMo app to show the exact timestamp the money was deducted. [1, 4, 5, 6, 7] 
